Together with John Giannandrea, Montulli wrote the initial Netscape cookie specification the same year. Version 0.9beta of , released on 13 October 1994, supported cookies. The first use of cookies (out of the labs) was checking whether visitors to the Netscape website had already visited the site. Montulli applied for a patent for the cookie technology in 1995, which was granted in 1998. Support for cookies was integrated with in version 2, released in October 1995.Together with John Giannandrea, Montulli wrote the initial Netscape cookie specification the same year. Version 0.9beta of Mosaic NetscapeMosaic Netscape, released on 13 October 1994,
